   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to certain\ndisabilities of university police officers appointed by the state university\nof New York",
    "basePrintNo": "S7519",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7519-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §363-a, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7519\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\ncertain disabilities of university police officers appointed by the\nstate university of New York\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to provide a heart presumption regarding\nimpairment similar to the same presumption other law enforcement offi-\ncers receive.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 3 of Section 363-A of the Retirement and\nSocial Security Law to include university police officers appointed by\nthe State University of New York in the definition of police officers\nsubject to the presumption that any disability or death resulting from\nheart disease was incurred in the performance and discharge of duty.\n\nSection 2 states that amendments made to Section 363-A of the Retirement\nand Social Security Law by this act do not affect the application of\nsuch provisions as extended by the provisions of\n\nSection 480 of the Retirement and Social Security Law.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUniversity police officers appointed by the State University of New York\nperform duties which are as stressful and physically demanding as other\npolice officers and firefighters. This bill will provide SUNY police\nofficers with the same benefit that pertains to a heart presumption as\nprovided to other police officers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: A.4393-A - Reported Referred to Ways and Means\n\n2020: S.8007 - Referred to Civil Service and Pensions/A.9876 - Referred\nto Governmental Employees\n\n2019: 5.3481 - Vetoed Memo. 265/A.5301 - Vetoed Memo. 265\n\n2017-2018: S.4634-A - Vetoed Memo. 352/A.6413-A - Vetoed Memo. 352\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
